  "name": "UNSATURATED IRON BINDING CAPACITY (UIBC)",
  "code": "UIBC",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Parameter</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Normal Range</strong> (Adults)</th>\n<th><strong>Increased UIBC</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Decreased UIBC</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>UIBC</strong> (Unsaturated Iron Binding Capacity)</td>\n<td><strong>150 &ndash; 375 &micro;g/dL</strong> (may vary by lab)</td>\n<td>- Iron deficiency anemia (early stage) - Pregnancy - Acute/Chronic blood loss</td>\n<td>- Hemochromatosis (iron overload) - Hemolytic anemia - Chronic liver disease - Sideroblastic anemia - Chronic infections/inflammation</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<ul data-start=\"645\" data-end=\"1002\">\n<li data-start=\"645\" data-end=\"749\">\n<p data-start=\"647\" data-end=\"749\"><strong data-start=\"647\" data-end=\"655\">UIBC</strong> measures the <strong data-start=\"669\" data-end=\"712\">reserve binding capacity of transferrin</strong> (how much more iron it can carry).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"750\" data-end=\"1002\">\n<p data-start=\"752\" data-end=\"850\">It is typically interpreted <strong data-start=\"780\" data-end=\"847\">together with serum iron and TIBC (Total Iron Binding Capacity)</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"853\" data-end=\"1002\">\n<li data-start=\"853\" data-end=\"913\">\n<p data-start=\"855\" data-end=\"913\"><strong data-start=\"855\" data-end=\"911\">High UIBC + Low serum iron &rarr; Iron deficiency anemia.</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"916\" data-end=\"1002\">\n<p data-start=\"918\" data-end=\"1002\"><strong data-start=\"918\" data-end=\"1000\">Low UIBC + High serum iron &rarr; Iron overload conditions (e.g., hemochromatosis).</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"1004\" data-end=\"1153\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">&nbsp;</p>",
